# Proposed features recognized from mushroom.step by sidecar/import_step.py
# (contract v1 -- see sidecar/CONTRACT.md). Review before use:
# recognition proposes, it does not machine.

# F1: outer profile under top cap F3: vertical wall loop F1 F2 F6 F4, top at z=14.0, base at z=6.0, material inside the loop; the base at z=6.0 is the head's own underside (the face under the walls faces down): the wall is traced from above, the underside is the other setup's (CHECKLIST row 2.2)
# consume with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F1_Profile, comp=control)  [the feature carries its own z + extent]
# the loop is wound CW: material inside, tool outside (the winding convention,
# DECISIONS.md -> "Row-2.4 side selector")
# comp=control is required on Contour runs: recognized boundaries carry rounded
# corners tessellated to chords, and engine comp hard-errors on rounded-corner
# offsets (DECISIONS.md -> "recognized contours propose comp=control")
# the base at z=6.0 is an overhang: the face under the walls faces down, so the
# tool has air under it at the base; the underside itself is the other setup's
feature F1_Profile ProfileBoss(z=14.0, extent=8.0
    10.0 10.0
    10.0 50.0
    50.0 50.0
    50.0 10.0
)

# F3: planar, normal +Z, topmost planar face (CHECKLIST row 1.1)
feature F3_Top Plane(z=14.0)
